{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they shall swoop.</b> Some say it is like מגילה עפה (Zechariah 5:1), unfolded. R. Moses the Kohen says it has no [parallel] like it, and the meaning is like ינוחו, and it lacks a [parallel] place in the land:" "<b>Westward.</b> For they are the west of the land of Israel:" "<b>The children of the east.</b> They are the Arameans:" "<b>The sending forth of their hand.</b> That they will send forth their hand to plunder them:" "<b>And the children of Ammon their obedience.</b> They shall come under their obedience:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מקום ארץ' is obscure; possibly 'a place [of comparison] in [the] land [of Hebrew],' i.e., no parallel usage in biblical Hebrew. Translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:29.914204273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}